Exercise: sa-scripts-review (chapter 15 lab)

Work on servera, with sudo or as root.

The script
 1. /usr/local/bin/sa-report.sh, a bash script (first line #!/bin/bash,
    mode 755) that takes one argument, a directory, and prints three lines:
        Directory: NAME
        Files: N        (regular files directly inside it)
        Bytes: N        (their total size in bytes)
    and exits with status 0.
    - With no argument (or more than one), it prints a line starting with
      "Usage: " to standard error and exits with status 2.
    - If the argument is not a directory, it prints a message containing
      "not a directory" to standard error and exits with status 1.
    The grader runs it as an ordinary user, so it must work without root.

Scheduling
 2. /etc/cron.d/sa-report: run "/usr/local/bin/sa-report.sh /etc/ssh" as
    root at 06:15 on weekdays (Monday to Friday). You may append the output
    to /var/log/sa-report.log.
 3. A personal crontab for student with a heartbeat every 10 minutes:
        /usr/bin/logger -t sa-heartbeat alive
 4. A systemd service sa-report.service (Type=oneshot) running
    "/usr/local/bin/sa-report.sh /etc", and a timer sa-report.timer that
    starts it daily at 02:30, with Persistent=true. The timer must be
    enabled and running.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-scripts-review
